  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The rate of change of the particle's $y$-coordinate when $t=2$ is given by ${y}^{′}(2).$\n\nIn step 5, we found that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3-3{t}^{2}}{t({t}^{2}+3)}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{3-3(2)^{2}}{2({2}^{2}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-12}{2(7)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{14}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
